Also try an undefined cmavo, such as "mi'oi":

mi'oi bu
text
   buClauseNoPre
   |- CMAVO
   |     cmavo: mi'oi
   |- CMAVO
         BU: bu

> -> fa'o bu
>    [ shouldn't and doesn't parse ]

Actually it should parse; it's equivalent to the null string. If I type a 
valid sentence followed by "fa'o", it handles it the same way; everything up 
to "fa'o" is output, and the "fa'o" is dropped.

